{"step_index":6460,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T10:52:19Z","thinking":"Encountered an \"Access is denied\" error when attempting to terminate a process. The hypothesis is to leverage a specific Windows API that can execute commands with elevated privileges, prompting the user for confirmation. This approach would allow forceful process termination, which is necessary to free up ports. This will be implemented as a helper method.\n\n\nFirst attempt is to use the standard `taskkill` command to terminate the processes, retrying with an elevated command via a specific Windows API if the standard attempt fails, indicating a permissions issue. This should reliably free the target ports. The approach uses `netstat` to identify the process ID (PID) associated with the ports.\n\n```batch\n@echo off\nfor %%a in (8000 8001) do (\n  for /f \"tokens=5\" %%b in ('netstat -ano ^| findstr \":%%a \" ^| find \"LISTENING\"') do (\n    taskkill /F /PID %%b\n  )\n)\n```\nThe batch script automates this port-killing process, iterating through the specified ports and forcefully terminating listening processes using the same logic as the Python implementation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"Set-Content -Path \"scripts\\free_ports.bat\" -Value \"@echo off`r`ntitle تحرير منافذ السيرفرات - فارما ماتش`r`necho ========================================================`r`necho    إغلاق أي عمليات معلقة على المنافذ 8000 و 8001`r`necho ========================================================`r`npowershell -NoProfile -Command `\"Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 8000,8001 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id `$_.OwningProcess -Force }`\"`r`necho.`r`necho [+] تم تحرير المنافذ بنجاح!`r`npause\" -Encoding UTF8","Cwd":"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Creating free_ports.bat script","toolSummary":"Create scripts/free_ports.bat"}}]}
